      "item": "theoreticalsciences:contact_process_tower",
      "title": "Contact Process Tower",
      "text": "Sulfur dioxide and air over three beds of vanadium catalyst, cooled between them, and the sulfur trioxide absorbed into acid.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 1$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the bed temperature and the oxygen excess. Below 670 K the vanadium does nothing; hotter it is faster, but the equilibrium falls back. A pass must convert 95%. More oxygen pushes the equilibrium on but dilutes the gas. Above 873 K the bed sinters. Needs a Vanadium Bed in its catalyst slot."
    },
